  "body": "Task: SF-A29-T05.7\nRelated: #1149\n\n## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nIL assembly appended every body even when the complete visible document was unchanged. That changed the embedded image on every format/assemble/format cycle and invalidated debug/signature fields without a corresponding body edit.\n\nThe image writer now compiles and validates every required visible method, then compares exact code bytes, maximum stack, locals token, initialization state and ordered exception clauses. Unchanged bodies retain their RVAs and physical encodings; actual changes use the existing append and invalidation path. When neither bodies nor the user-string heap change, the result owns a byte-identical copy of the original image.\n\nThis preserves compact body/EH encodings, metadata, resources, padding, checksums and existing signature/debug bytes for an unchanged document. It does not authenticate signatures. Missing methods and invalid operands, locals, exception ranges, options or image layout remain errors.\n\nNegative zero is formatted explicitly. A validated NaN at a matching original label and exact floating opcode retains only its original four/eight operand bytes; other instructions compile normally. Finite, width or label edits use the appropriate new encoding. The final body comparison remains exact.\n\n## Stronger fuzz property\n\nThe adapter now compares the complete canonical document, including .image, and reports IL_DOCUMENT_EXACT_ROUNDTRIP. Generated-text errors and inequality remain findings. The authored seeds include negative zero and a noncanonical NaN payload. Historical visible-text evidence retains its narrower scope.\n\nThe old managed-IL regression expected debug-profile invalidation even without a body change. It now makes an explicit 42→43 edit before requiring invalidation, alongside new unchanged-image preservation tests.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Parent source 8019f2f9b22e26d7c221454f3b751b0b0e0c67df with the two new public test files: 14 tests, 2 pass and 12 fail.\n- Final focused batch: 124 pass, zero failures, skips or cancellations.\n- Includes both new A03 files, existing managed IL, layout and strings, text targets and protocol sequences. The public execution regressions exercise source-profile and direct CIL VM routes.\n- Exact-image CLI campaign: seed 1, 32 cases, 7 accepted and 25 controlled rejections, zero findings/unsupported/cancellations; clean source before and after.\n- Independent source, seed, documentation and test-expectation review found no blocker.\n- New source files meet size/line limits; the frozen public il-document.js shrinks from 51 to 34 lines.\n- Tests/campaign ran serially on Linux x64 with Node24.19.0. Ordinary core does not execute Node tests.\n\nTested local commit: 9e6235635fdfb92939e8d7cbf1985db774d1fa31.\nPublished implementation commit: 7ae8ae6727f627be4cd63c56099814f5004f9c29.\nExact tested/published tree: 3b4b42b335f088d800610ad4af19dafde9fa07a3.\n\n## Changes outside this workstream\n\nThese minimal CIL image/body/formatter corrections are prerequisites for the A29 round-trip property. All 98 live claim records and the relevant issue-specific ownership sections were reread. The nine reserved A03 metadata leaves and table-width test remain untouched; the edited leaves had no exact reservation. The existing public format export and compile API remain compatible.\n\nThe added comparisons and NaN indexing are linear in code, instructions and exception clauses. No measured performance improvement is claimed. Native CLR, browsers, Rust, general metadata editing and Microsoft ilasm compatibility remain separate qualification/capability obligations. #1149 remains open for its remaining acceptance scope.",
